            "encryptedReviewData": "s58V6axpmmFBTJDT1oz62Q==",
            "formattedRating": "3.2",
            "formattedReviewDate": "May 18, 2026",
            "formattedReviewHelpfulText": "Did you find this review helpful?",
            "ratingText": "Review score",
            "responderName": "Hotel Vendome",
            "responseDateText": "",
            "responseTranslateSource": "zh-CN",
            "reviewComments": "The hotel’s location was okay, and there weren’t many guests, but the rooms are extremely poorly soundproofed. I could clearly hear people talking next door, and their child even came and knocked on my door at 11 p.m. The worst part was the door lock: the turning handle was broken, and whenever I left the room, I had to put the key into the upper deadbolt and turn it to lock the door.\n\nAt over SGD 400 a night, housekeeping didn’t change the sheets or towels, or replenish the drinking water or coffee. The bin liner was fitted so badly that as soon as I threw something away, it slipped down to the bottom of the bin, making it as though there were no liner at all—the rubbish went straight into the bin. The wardrobe’s sliding door wouldn’t move and had a strange smell.\n\nThe reception staff were fairly polite, but the housekeeping staff didn’t even greet me. I absolutely would not recommend staying at this hotel.",
            "reviewNegatives": "",
            "reviewPositives": "",
            "reviewProviderLogo": "",
            "reviewProviderText": "Agoda",
            "reviewTitle": "Poor value for money; outdated facilities.",
            "translateSource": "zh-CN",
            "translateTarget": "en",
